1
00:00:00,179 --> 00:00:03,805
Picture a product information system rolled out as a project.

2
00:00:04,025 --> 00:00:07,908
The go-live happens, the project closes, and the team is reassigned.

3
00:00:08,128 --> 00:00:12,181
Six months later the product data is out of date, because nobody owns it.

4
00:00:12,401 --> 00:00:16,135
That is what treating a product like a project looks like in practice.

5
00:00:16,885 --> 00:00:18,463
Three things to do this week.

6
00:00:18,683 --> 00:00:22,097
One: name an owner for the outcome, not just the delivery.

7
00:00:22,317 --> 00:00:26,178
Two: set a review date after launch, and treat it as part of the work.

8
00:00:26,398 --> 00:00:30,537
Three: define success in customer terms, not in tasks completed.

9
00:00:30,757 --> 00:00:33,829
That is the shift from project thinking to product thinking.
